/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  dryer01_sucrose_tray / constant/components/sucrose.dat  --  PARTIAL OVERLAY.

  The GAB water-sorption isotherm is SAMPLE data: it belongs to THIS powder
  (amorphous/crystalline state, particle size, thermal history), not to the
  pure compound, so it lives in the case and merges field-by-field over the
  standards record (MW, Cp, rho_p, solubility all come from there).  Axiom 4
  of the property layout; `overlayOf` makes the patch explicit.

  PROVENANCE, stated rather than dressed up: these are the SAME three
  numbers the sugar-drying corpus already carries for its teaching sample
  (solidDryer01_sugar, the sprayDryer family, the plant tutorials), so the
  batch drying curve and the steady dryers answer to ONE isotherm and cannot
  drift apart.  That set carries NO primary citation anywhere in the tree,
  and inventing one here would turn `unsourced` into `falsely sourced` --
  a visible gap is strictly better than an invisible falsehood.  It is a
  plausible teaching isotherm for a sugar solid; no number in this case is
  validated against measurement.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

overlayOf      sucrose;

sorption
{
    Xm   0.045;     // GAB monolayer moisture      [kg/kg dry solid]
    C    6.0;       // GAB energy constant         [-]
    K    0.96;      // GAB multilayer factor       [-]
}
